h could narrow the margin, though not plausibly enough to threaten the outcome.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Newest usable poll is 52 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Wes Moore (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Wes Moore seeks a second term against Republican Dan Cox, whom he defeated in 2022, in a state that leans Democratic by 15 points. Moore enters with strong fundamentals: a 56% approval rating, a dominant fundraising edge of more than $15 million raised to Cox's $240,000, and a 58-31 lead in the most recent poll of likely voters.\n\nAll six expert ratings call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Moore's chances at 97% or higher. Cox has campaigned on electricity costs and data-center issues, and the two will debate in October, but the structural advantages favor Moore heavily. The main uncertainty is the age of the polling, which widens the error band without changing the expected outcome.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9967, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}]}